            "commit": "c9a79a8950c5cb958f6e03f66f0817d34bed9553",
            "subject": "LU-17000 lnet: fix double free when adding a duplicate NI"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Oleg Drokin",
          "email": "green@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-09-09 05:13:40.000000000",
          "tz": -240
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Oleg Drokin",
          "email": "green@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-09-10 04:43:32.000000000",
          "tz": -240
        },
        "subject": "LU-17000 lnet: fix use-after-free in lnet_add_net_common()",
        "message": "LU-17000 lnet: fix use-after-free in lnet_add_net_common()\n\nlnet_startup_lndnet() consumes the net it is given: on success it\neither links it into the_lnet.ln_nets or, when its NIs were merged\ninto an already existing net, frees it.  lnet_add_net_common()\nlooks the live net up again by id for that reason, but the\nlnet_ping_target_setup() failure branch runs before that lookup\nand hands the stale pointer to lnet_shutdown_lndnet().  Adding an\ninterface to an existing net, e.g. \"lnetctl net add --net tcp --if\neth1\" while tcp is up, faults there when the ping buffer cannot be\nallocated.\n\nSet the ping buffer up after the lookup, so that no error path can\nreach the consumed pointer.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-lnet\nFixes: db0fb8f2b649 (\"LU-10391 lnet: allow ping packet to contain large nids\")\nSigned-off-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5 llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I9a6a8bd1c8f4500339026b5eab00cb47d00aadd2\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
